# Documentation maintenance rules

This repo has a generated documentation set under `docs/` and `codebase-analysis-docs/`, plus a root `CLAUDE.md` context file. These are living documents, not a one-time snapshot — treat drift between docs and code as a bug.

## Before a large refactor or cross-cutting change

1. Read [`codebase-analysis-docs/CODEBASE_KNOWLEDGE.md`](../../codebase-analysis-docs/CODEBASE_KNOWLEDGE.md) — it documents the load-bearing architectural patterns (transactional outbox, reconciliation-never-creates-a-charge, idempotency-by-DB-constraint) and known gotchas.
2. Read [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for the relevant subsystem's design before changing it.
3. Check [`docs/DATA_MODELS.md`](../../docs/DATA_MODELS.md) before adding/changing a Prisma model or a field with a non-obvious invariant.

## When touching a core module

Core modules: anything under `src/app/api/webhooks/`, `src/lib/jobs/`, `src/lib/reconciliation/`, `src/lib/finix/`, `src/lib/auth/`, or anything that creates/mutates a `Payment`, `InvoicePayment`, or `RefundRequest`.

- If your change alters the *behavior* documented in [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), [`docs/API.md`](../../docs/API.md), [`docs/DATA_MODELS.md`](../../docs/DATA_MODELS.md), or [`docs/AUTHENTICATION.md`](../../docs/AUTHENTICATION.md), update the relevant section in the same change — don't leave it for later.
- If you're not sure whether a change is documentation-worthy, at minimum flag it in your response to the user rather than silently letting the docs go stale.
- New environment variables must be added to [`docs/CONFIGURATION.md`](../../docs/CONFIGURATION.md).
- New API routes worth documenting (i.e. not a thin CRUD wrapper already covered by the folder-level index in `docs/API.md`) should get an entry there.

## Style for new documentation

- Match the existing tone: direct, assumes a competent developer joining the project, explains *why* not just *what*.
- Cross-link instead of duplicating — if a concept is already explained in another doc, link to it rather than re-explaining it.
- Prefer updating an existing doc's section over creating a new file, unless the topic is genuinely a new cross-cutting concern (in which case, add it to the documentation map in root `CLAUDE.md` too).
- Keep [`codebase-analysis-docs/CODEBASE_KNOWLEDGE.md`](../../codebase-analysis-docs/CODEBASE_KNOWLEDGE.md)'s "Documentation TODO" section current — remove items once addressed, add newly-discovered gaps.
